WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:06.010
Now let's see how to add a new talk from Amruta.

2
00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.940
We have the "+ Add Talk" button.

3
00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.940
If we click it, we will see a hint:

4
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:19.080
"Drag this button to your bookmarks bar, then click it

5
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.620
while on a talk page at amruta.org." Let's try it.

6
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.480
We open the bookmarks bar.

7
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:32.460
Mine is here; it can differ: by default it is at the top, and in general,

8
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.880
find some bookmarks bar or bookmarks list.

9
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.000
I already have it here, so I'll delete it

10
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:45.120
and drag it into the bookmarks.

11
00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:50.900
Here we just click "Save" – and we have this bookmark.

12
00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.780
Now we need to go to the Amruta page.

13
00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:00.180
I'll use this feature here.

14
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:06.760
By clicking the date. And let's take "Talk of the day",

15
00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:13.110
the first one we came across.

16
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.920
Here there is "Review transcript".

17
00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:19.660
Here there are subtitles.

18
00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:24.170
Excellent.

19
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.340
What do we do now?

20
00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:33.760
While on this Amruta page, we click our "+ Sahaja Yoga Subtitles".

21
00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:39.100
When we click it, a page like this opens.

22
00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:46.640
It is already prefilled: it automatically picked up which videos there are, which

23
00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:53.560
transcript, and here even an encoded view

24
00:01:54.720 --> 00:02:01.500
of this transcript. These are technical things; it has to be like this for it all to work.

25
00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:08.960
What do we do now? We click the green "Create PR" button. By this point we

26
00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.280
should already be registered on GitHub.

27
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:18.980
What does it say here? "meta.yaml copied. Click "Open GitHub", then paste

28
00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:22.160
(Ctrl+V) into the new file content field."

29
00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:24.280
Let's go through this procedure together.

30
00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:27.100
First – "Open GitHub".

31
00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:34.500
Second – we put the cursor here and pressed Ctrl+V or

32
00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:40.480
"Paste". And after that we click the green button.

33
00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:47.190
We need to click the green one several times.

34
00:02:55.660 --> 00:03:02.320
Three green ones. That is the whole adding procedure on your side.

35
00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:09.170
Once that is done, you can simply take this link and send it to me, so that

36
00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:14.890
I can then start that costly

37
00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:20.910
translation process, which is tied

38
00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:24.190
to a private paid subscription at the moment.

39
00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:32.360
On your side, apart from these three buttons, you don't need to click anything else here

40
00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:37.540
at all. Just take this link or the number and simply say

41
00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:42.880
in a private message: here, please, we need…

42
00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:47.580
we want to work on translating this one.

43
00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:55.020
So your part ends at this point.

44
00:03:55.240 --> 00:04:00.580
I'm not talking about cases where someone also takes on these tasks and

45
00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:04.820
runs these translations on their own subscriptions.

46
00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:09.750
But for transparency I can show what happens next.

47
00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:14.150
You sent me this link – I opened it.

48
00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.650
And what do I do first?

49
00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:22.630
I wait while these yellow automatic processes here are running, so that they

50
00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:28.870
finish. What is here? There is unpacking, fetching the subtitles,

51
00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:34.930
in general certain technical processes; once they are finished,

52
00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:41.470
part of the automatic processes will be done.

53
00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:48.430
The ones we can run for free, because this platform,

54
00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:54.920
GitHub, gives us some computing power for free.

55
00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:58.550
They will run here; I'll wait until it is all done.

56
00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:02.330
And after it finishes,

57
00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:07.290
I'll accept it and click this "Merge" button.

58
00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:15.430
These changes will get into the system, and after that I'll go and start this

59
00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:21.510
subtitle pipeline, where I'll enter the name, for example,

60
00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:29.260
this was your name, and, basically, click this green

61
00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:33.440
button. Then a process like this one will start,

62
00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:37.250
in which the translation will happen,

63
00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:44.930
the translation will be checked by proofreading, by a linguist, by an agent that creates

64
00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:46.370
subtitles, and so on.

65
00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:51.690
If it fails somewhere – I'll check whether it is a system error or a peculiarity of that

66
00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:57.090
talk. And if it is green,

67
00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:04.780
then on this portal this talk

68
00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:08.920
will automatically appear under "Needs review".

69
00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:12.970
We won't wait now for all these processes to run,

70
00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:20.130
but in general this is the procedure, for a full understanding of what

71
00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:26.610
happens. As you can see, this system lets you follow who proposed what change,

72
00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.150
and how the processes went.

73
00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.790
It is a kind of construction kit, you could say,

74
00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:40.430
which we assembled for our needs and we work with it. That's all

75
00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:42.470
on adding a new talk.
